{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For you have come</b> — even though, as in: for [he] rode iron [chariot]; for [it is] a stiff-necked people." "<b>In the palm</b> — in his authority, as in: from what comes into his hand. Soften yourself, from 'her foot softened' (רפסה). And the meaning: go to him and humble yourself, and let yourself be trampled." "<b>And urge</b> — participle, and it is the cause: cleave to your friend."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:08.551788664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}